pelt_args=-i -m
prompt_wait=5
tr_by=hand
why=sh37, pelt#114: PAX's shapes line, eight `true &` and a `wait` in an interactive job-control shell, prints its SHAPE line and a prompt comes back within 5 s, three times; then two lines of a hundred rounds of it, then a `wait` that must park (`sleep 1 &`). At wolf 0.2.36 the forks can end the runtime's signal drain thread, and a wait that parks after that never wakes: the last step is the one that hangs once the thread is gone, wherever it went. The ended jobs are told of at the next prompt (standard error). Written by hand; dash 0.5.13.4 -i -m prints the same standard output (paced by quiet, its last line lands one step later: the 1 s sleep outlasts the pause)
